bqQ","user":{"login":"BaconEggsRL","id":18596035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk2MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18596035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL","html_url":"https://github.com/BaconEggsRL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-17T21:47:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T21:47:25Z","body":"> The change here seems fine.\r\n> \r\n> But why does the presence of a LightOccluder2D make the issue go away?\r\n\r\nI believe the presence of the LightOccluder2D with SDF collision enabled causes the shader to find solid pixels in the SDF calculation.\r\n\r\nSo the value of p_float would be the (normalized) distance to the nearest point of the occluder geometry.\r\n\r\nWithout the occluder, there is no solid collision geometry for the calculation in LOAD step.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6241721257/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6242096050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124564#issuecomment-6242096050","issue_url":"ht